  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Calculate $F(3)$ where $F(x)={\\int }_{0}^{x}\\sqrt{t}\\,\\text{d}t.$",
  "worked_solution": "Evaluating $F(x)$ at $x=3,$ we get the following definite integral:\n\n$$\nF(3)={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{t}\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nThen, computing the definite integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(3) & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{t}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\frac{2}{3}{t}^{3/2}|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}({3}^{3/2}-{0}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(({3}^{3})^{1/2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{27} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 3\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
